                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of quisling."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "05158b70-43c6-45d3-8b2f-22266e3cb853",
                                "sense_id": "4c8eab9d-b379-3138-8e24-43a60c532742",
                                "text": "Other potential \"quislers\" still at large last week include: Sweden's Sven Olav Lindholm, an Army sergeant who willingly dubs himself Sweden's Hitler; Holland's Blackshirt Anton Adrian Missert; Hungary's Greenshirt Kalman Hubay; England's Blackshirt Sir Oswald Mosley; Belgium's broom-waving Rexist Léon Degrelle and the underground pro-Nazi conspirators who agitate in Alsace-Lorraine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed5f23f4-1c17-4829-b9fc-4dced1c16486",
                                "sense_id": "4c8eab9d-b379-3138-8e24-43a60c532742",
                                "text": "The capture of the fleet would have been its delivery “to the enemy,” for France now knows and even the Vichy government knows—except Laval and a dwindling coterie of his fellow quislers—that Germany is the enemy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1b2647d-3ff5-4d90-9027-599599efcf11",
                                "sense_id": "4c8eab9d-b379-3138-8e24-43a60c532742",
                                "text": "In the rumblings of mounting war sentiment, the radicals and the left-wing trade unions blended in the public imagination into a diffuse mass of pacifist quislers, immigrants of shaky loyalties, and anarchist saboteurs."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
